<title>BELGIUM: Solvay trade frozen after mistrade.</title>
<headline>Solvay trade frozen after mistrade.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade in the shares of Belgian chemical firm Solvay was temporarily halted on the Brussels bourse early on Tuesday after a mistrade, a trader said.</p>
<p>&quot;Apparently there was a mistrade and the stock has been frozen. But it is not suspended,&quot; the trader said.</p>
<p>A spokesman for the Brussels Stock Exchange said trade would resume at 0956 GMT after the mistrade.</p>
<p>Solvay last traded at 22,300 francs, up 25 from Monday's close having moved in an early 22,475/22,200 francs range.</p>
